{
  "title": "74: Al-Muddaththir المدثر",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُۙ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL MUDDASSER.\nO you wrapped up in your mantle!\nقُمْ فَاَنْذِرْۙ‏(2)\nQUM FA-ANZIR.\nRise up and warn!\nوَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْۙ‏(3)\nWA RABBAKA FA-KABBIR.\nMagnify your Lord,\nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْۙ‏(4)\nWA SEYAABAKA FA-TAHHIR.\nand purify your clothes,\nوَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْۙ‏(5)\nWAR RUJZA FAHJUR.\nand keep away from all impurity!\nوَلَا تَمْنُنْ تَسْتَكْثِرُۙ‏(6)\nWA LAA TAMNUN TASTAKSER.\nDo not grant a favour seeking a greater gain,\nوَ لِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْؕ‏(7)\nWA LE-RABBEKA FASBIR.\nand be patient for the sake of your Lord.\nفَاِذَا نُقِرَ فِى النَّاقُوْرِۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAA NOQERA FIN NAAQOOR.\nWhen the Trumpet will be sounded,\nفَذٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوْمٌ عَسِيْرٌۙ‏(9)\nFAZAALEKA YAWMA-EZIN-Y YAWMUN A’SEER.\nthat will be a day of hardship,\nعَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ غَيْرُ يَسِيْرٍ‏(10)\nA’LAL KAAFEREENA GHAYRO YASEER.\nnot at all easy for the faithless.\nذَرْنِىْ وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيْدًا ۙ‏(11)\nZARNEE WA MAN KHALAQTO WAHEEDAA.\nLeave Me [to deal] with him whom I created alone,\nوَّجَعَلْتُ لَهٗ مَالًا مَّمْدُوْدًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA JA-A’LTO LAHU MAALAM MAMDOODAA.\nand furnished him with extensive means,\nوَّبَنِيْنَ شُهُوْدًا ۙ‏(13)\nWA BANEENA SHOHOODAA.\n[gave him] sons to be at his side,\nوَّمَهَّدتُّ لَهٗ تَمْهِيْدًا ۙ‏(14)\nWA MAHHATTO LAHU TAMHEEDAA.\nand facilitated [all matters] for him.\nثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ اَنْ اَزِيْدَ  ۙ‏(15)\nSUMMA YATMA-O’ AN AZEED.\nStill he is eager that I should give him more.\nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِاٰيٰتِنَا عَنِيْدًا ؕ‏(16)\nKALLAA, INNAHU KAANA LE-AAYAATENAA A’NEEDAA.\nNo indeed! He is an obstinate opponent of Our signs.\nسَاُرْهِقُهٗ صَعُوْدًا ؕ‏(17)\nSA-URHEQOHU SA-O’ODAA.\nSoon I will overwhelm him with hardship.\nاِنَّهٗ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَۙ‏(18)\nINNAHU FAKKARA WA QADDAR.\nIndeed he reflected and decided.\nفَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(19)\nFA-QOTELA KAYFA QADDAR.\nPerish he, how he decided!\nثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(20)\nSUMMA QOTELA KAYFA QADDAR.\nAgain, perish he, how he decided!\nثُمَّ نَظَرَۙ‏(21)\nSUMMA NAZAR.\nThen he looked;\nثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَۙ‏(22)\nSUMMA A’BASA WA BASAR.\nthen frowned and scowled.\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَۙ‏(23)\nSUMMA ADBARA WAS TAKBAR.\nThen he walked away disdainfully,\nفَقَالَ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُّؤْثَرُۙ‏(24)\nFA-QAALA IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUN-Y YOASAR.\nsaying, ‘It is nothing but traditional sorcery.\nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِؕ‏(25)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA QAWLUL BASHAR.\nIt is nothing but the speech of a human.’\nسَاُصْلِيْهِ سَقَرَ‏(26)\nSA-USLEEHE SAQAR.\nSoon I will cast him into Saqar.\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سَقَرُؕ‏(27)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA SAQAR.\nAnd what will show you what is Saqar?\nلَا تُبْقِىْ وَ لَا تَذَرُۚ‏(28)\nLAA TUBQEE WA LAA TAZAR.\nIt neither spares, nor leaves [anything].\nلَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِۖۚ‏(29)\nLAWWAAHATUL LIL-BASHAR.\nIt burns the skin.\nعَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَؕ‏(30)\nA’LAYHAA TIS-A’TA A’SHAR.\nThere are nineteen [keepers] over it.\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَاۤ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اِلَّا مَلٰٓئِكَةً وَّمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ۙ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِيْمَانًا وَّلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ وَلِيَقُوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْكٰفِرُوْنَ مَاذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا مَثَلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُوْدَ رَبِّكَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ وَمَا هِىَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْبَشَرِ‏(31)\nWA MAA JA-A’LNAA ASHAABAN NAARE ILLAA MALAAA-EKAH, WA MAA JA-A’LNAA I’DDATAHUM ILLAA FITNATAL LILLAZEENA KAFAROO, LE-YASTAYQENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WA YAZDAADAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EEMAANANW WA LAA YARTAABAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WAL MOAMENOONA, WA LE-YAQOOLAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUNW WAL KAAFEROONA MAAZAA ARAADAL LAAHO BEHAAZAA MASALAA, KAZAALEKA YOZILLUL LAAHO MAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN-Y YASHAAA, WA MAA YA’LAMO JONOODA RABBEKA ILLAA HOO, WA MAA HEYA ILLAA ZIKRAA LIL-BASHAR.\nWe have assigned only angels as keepers of the Fire, and We have made their number merely a stumbling block for the faithless, and so that those who were given the Book may be reassured, and the faithful may increase in [their] faith, and so that those who were given the Book and the faithful may not be in doubt, and so that the faithless and those in whose hearts is a sickness may say, ‘What did Allah mean by this description?’ Thus does Allah lead astray whomever He wishes and guides whomever He wishes. No one knows the hosts of your Lord except Him, and it is just an admonition for all humans.\nكَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِۙ‏(32)\nKALLAA WAL QAMAR.\nNo indeed! By the Moon!\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذْ اَدْبَرَۙ‏(33)\nWAL LAYLE IZ ADBAR.\nBy the night when it recedes!\nوَالصُّبْحِ اِذَاۤ اَسْفَرَۙ‏(34)\nWAS SUBHE EZAA ASFAR.\nBy the dawn when it brightens!\nاِنَّهَا لَاِحْدَى الْكُبَرِۙ‏(35)\nINNAHAA LA-EHDAL KOBAR.\nIndeed they are one of the greatest [signs of God]\nنَذِيْرًا لِّلْبَشَرِۙ‏(36)\nNAZEERAL LIL-BASHAR.\n—a warner to all humans,\nلِمَنْ شَآءَ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ يَّتَقَدَّمَ اَوْ يَتَاَخَّرَؕ‏(37)\nLEMAN SHAAA-A MINKUM AN-Y YATAQADDAMA AW YATA-AKH-KHAR.\n[alike] for those of you who like to advance ahead and those who would remain behind.\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِيْنَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\nKULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT RAHEENAH.\nEvery soul is hostage to what it has earned,\nاِلَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ الْيَمِيْنِۛ ؕ‏(39)\nILLAA ASHAABAL YAMEEN.\nexcept the People of the Right Hand.\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ ۛ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۙ‏(40)\nFEE JANNAAT, YATASAAA-ALOON.\n[They will be] in gardens, questioning\nعَنِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(41)\nA’NIL MUJREMEEN.\nthe guilty:\nمَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِىْ سَقَرَ‏(42)\nMAA SALAKAKUM FEE SAQAR.\n‘What drew you into Hell?’\nقَالُوْا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(43)\nQAALOO LAM NAKO MENAL MOSALLEEN.\nThey will answer, ‘We were not among those who prayed.\nوَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWA LAM NAKO NUT-E’MUL MISKEEN.\nNor did we feed the poor.\nوَكُنَّا نَخُوْضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nWA KUNNAA NAKHOOZO MA-A’L KHAAA-EZEEN.\nWe used to indulge in [profane] gossip along with the gossipers,\nوَ كُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(46)\nWA KUNNAA NOKAZZEBO BE-YAWMID DEEN.\nand we used to deny the Day of Retribution\nحَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮنَا الْيَقِيْنُؕ‏(47)\nHATTAA ATAANAL YAQEEN.\nuntil death came to us.’\nفَمَا تَنْفَعُهُمْ شَفَاعَةُ الشّٰفِعِيْنَؕ‏(48)\nFAMAA TANFA-O’HUM SHAFAA-A’TUSH SHAAFE-E’EN.\nSo the intercession of the intercessors will not avail them.\nفَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(49)\nFAMAA LAHUM A’NIT TAZKERATE MO’REZEEN.\nWhat is the matter with them that they evade the Reminder\nكَاَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(50)\nKA-ANNAHUM HOMORUM MUSTANFERAH.\nas if they were terrified asses\nفَرَّتْ مِنْ قَسْوَرَةٍ ؕ‏(51)\nFARRAT MIN QASWARAH.\nfleeing from a lion?\nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ كُلُّ امْرِئٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّؤْتٰى صُحُفًا مُّنَشَّرَةً ۙ‏(52)\nBAL YOREEDO KULLUM RE-IM MINHUM AN-Y YOATAA SOHOFAM MONASH-SHARAH.\nBut everyone of them desires to be given unrolled scriptures [from Allah]!\nكَلَّا ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَخَافُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(53)\nKALLAA, BAL LAA YAKHAAFOONAL AAKHERAH.\nNo! Indeed, they do not fear the Hereafter.\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهٗ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(54)\nKALLAA INNAHU TAZKERAH.\nNo! It is indeed a reminder.\nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ ؕ‏(55)\nFAMAN SHAAA-A ZAKARAH.\nSo let anyone who wishes be mindful of it.\nوَمَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ هُوَ اَهْلُ التَّقْوٰى وَاَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‏(56)\nWA MAA YAZKOROONA ILLAA AN-Y YASHAAA-AL LAAH, HOWA AHLUT TAQWAA WA AHLUL MAGHFERAH.\nAnd they will not be mindful unless Allah wishes. He is worthy of [your] being wary [of Him] and He is worthy to forgive.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Muddassir (The Clothed One)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 56 verses. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah in his compulsory prayers will attain a rank near the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in the hereafter and will be protected from any misfortunes in this world.\nIf this Surah is recited daily and then a dua is made after its recitation, then the dua will be answered and the need will be fulfilled. If one makes dua that he wishes to memorize the whole Qur’an then he will not die until he has memorized it."
}
